This folder contains an operator that can be used with an airflow client
To have this operator deployed 
- Airflow should be already installed in your machine and running.
- All the library needed for your operator should be already installed in your machine
- Configure the Worker as Airflow worker. For doing so:
    - Add in config.json: worker."container_management" : "airflow"
    - Add docker-compose.yml (change /tmp/* to your local folders): 
        - /tmp/airflow_home:/airflow_home      
        - /tmp/localpyrepo:/local_pymodules_repository
- Put the content of this folder (starting from "dummymodulde-1.0.0" into the chosen /tmp/localpyrepo/. 
    - First option: You put the folder as it is with the whole structure. So you can change the content and the folder is newly taked for each deployment
    - Second option: You compress the folder as zip file and put the zip file "dummymodulde-1.0.0.zip" into the localpyrepo folder. In this way you can have releases of it. (but you need to create the zip file).
    PLEASE NOTE: in the first option, the zip file is created on the fly by the worker
